   "content": "Impute the missing `city` using the following rules, prioritized in order:\n\n1. **Phone Area Code (Primary Cue):** Map the 3-digit prefix of the `phone` field to its corresponding metropolitan area:\n   - `212`: new york (or new york city)\n   - `415`: san francisco\n   - `404`: atlanta\n   - `310`: marina del rey or west la (use address/name cues to distinguish; e.g., \"pico blvd\" maps to west la, \"washington blvd.\" maps to marina del rey).\n   - `702`: las vegas\n\n2. **Address Cues (Secondary Cue):** Check `addr` for prominent local street names, neighborhoods, or landmarks (e.g., \"las vegas blvd\" $\\rightarrow$ las vegas; \"hurt plaza\" or \"peachtree rd\" $\\rightarrow$ atlanta).\n\n3. **Granularity and Spelling:** \n   - Use standard, lowercase metropolitan names as shown in the examples (e.g., `new york`, `new york city`, `san francisco`, `las vegas`, `atlanta`, `marina del rey`, `west la`). \n   - Retain specific local abbreviations or colloquial designations when present in the convention (e.g., `west la` instead of full municipal names if supported by area code and street).",
