   "latency_s": 2.723,
   "content": "Impute the missing `city` value using the following rules, prioritized from highest to lowest:\n\n1. **Phone Area Code (Primary Cue):** Map the 3-digit area code from the `phone` field to its primary metropolitan city:\n   - `212`: `new york` (Note: \"new york city\" is also accepted for 212).\n   - `415`: `san francisco`.\n   - `404`: `atlanta`.\n   - `310`: `marina del rey` or `west la` (verify specific street/neighborhood against address if ambiguous).\n   - `702`: `las vegas`.\n\n2. **Address Cues (Secondary Cue):** Use specific street names, landmarks, or regional street suffixes in the `addr` field to refine or confirm the city:\n   - Manhattan street grids (e.g., numbered streets like \"w. 46th st.\", avenues like \"amsterdam ave.\") dictate `new york`.\n   - Major regional thoroughfares (e.g., \"pico blvd.\") help distinguish local sub-markets like `west la` from general Los Angeles area codes (`310`).\n   - Landmark plazas or regional road names (e.g., \"hurt plaza\", \"peachtree rd.\") dictate `atlanta`.\n   - Famous boulevards (e.g., \"las vegas blvd.\") dictate `las vegas`.\n\n3. **Spelling and Granularity:** \n   - Use lowercase letters exclusively for city names.\n   - Use standard municipal names (e.g., `new york`, `san francisco`, `atlanta`), but accept dataset-specific locality granularity when strongly cued (e.g., `marina del rey`, `west la`, or `new york city`).",
