   "latency_s": 68.287,
   "content": "### Imputation Rules for City Values\n\n1. **Las Vegas**:\n   - Use \"Las Vegas\" for addresses containing \"Las Vegas Blvd.\" or any part of the Las Vegas Strip.\n   - Example: \"3400 las vegas blvd. s\" \u2192 \"Las Vegas\"\n\n2. **San Francisco**:\n   - Use \"San Francisco\" for addresses in San Francisco, typically including streets like Hayes St., Steuart St., etc.\n   - Example: \"320 hayes st.\" \u2192 \"San Francisco\"\n\n3. **New York City**:\n   - Use \"New York\" for most addresses in Manhattan, such as W 67th St., Amsterdam Ave., W 46th St., and 1st Ave.\n   - Exception: For more specific areas like the Financial District or other distinct neighborhoods, use \"New York City.\"\n   - Example: \"86 w. third st.\" \u2192 \"New York City\"\n\n4. **Marina del Rey**:\n   - Use \"Marina del Rey\" for addresses in Marina del Rey, typically including Washington Blvd.\n   - Example: \"13329 washington blvd.\" \u2192 \"Marina del Rey\"\n\n5. **West LA**:\n   - Use \"West LA\" for addresses in the West Los Angeles area, such as W Pico Blvd.\n   - Example: \"10516 w. pico blvd.\" \u2192 \"West LA\"\n\n6. **Atlanta**:\n   - Use \"Atlanta\" for addresses in Atlanta, typically including streets like Hurt Plaza and Peachtree Rd.\n   - Example: \"3172 peachtree rd. ne\" \u2192 \"Atlanta\"\n\n### General Guidelines:\n- Always use the full city name as shown in the examples.\n- If an address is ambiguous or not clearly associated with a specific city, default to the most common city for that area code (e.g., 212 for New York).\n- For cities not listed here, use the closest major city or consult additional data sources.",
